From 2e1da88de8ba05c1f6b29047492a20dbcaebb634 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kieran Kunhya <kierank@obe.tv>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:04:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/hevc/mvs: test xB0 against the width before reading
 B0

AVAILABLE(cand_up_right, B0) reads the motion field at B0 before the
xB0 < width test. cand_up_right_sap is not limited to the picture
width, so at the right edge of a picture whose width is not a multiple
of the CTB size this reads the first entry of the next row, and the
result is then discarded. The read stays inside tab_mvf (PU offsets are
multiples of the minimum PU size, so the row is never the last one),
but there is no reason to make it.

Test the width first in the merge and the AMVP derivation. The result
of the condition is unchanged.

(cherry picked from commit 2e1da88de8ba05c1f6b29047492a20dbcaebb634)
Upstream: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/2e1da88de8ba05c1f6b29047492a20dbcaebb634
---
 libavcodec/hevc/mvs.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/mvs.c b/libavcodec/hevc/mvs.c
index 937c7cf..a14cfc6 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/mvs.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/mvs.c
@@ -368,8 +368,8 @@ static void derive_spatial_merge_candidates(HEVCLocalContext *lc, const HEVCCont
     }
 
     // above right spatial merge candidate
-    is_available_b0 = AVAILABLE(cand_up_right, B0) &&
-                      xB0 < sps->width &&
+    is_available_b0 = xB0 < sps->width &&
+                      AVAILABLE(cand_up_right, B0) &&
                       PRED_BLOCK_AVAILABLE(B0) &&
                       !is_diff_mer(pps, xB0, yB0, x0, y0);
 
@@ -689,8 +689,8 @@ b_candidates:
     xB0    = x0 + nPbW;
     yB0    = y0 - 1;
 
-    is_available_b0 =  AVAILABLE(cand_up_right, B0) &&
-                       xB0 < sps->width &&
+    is_available_b0 =  xB0 < sps->width &&
+                       AVAILABLE(cand_up_right, B0) &&
                        PRED_BLOCK_AVAILABLE(B0);
 
     // above spatial merge candidate
